{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mcneese/jobs/5509639/accounting-specialist": {
      "title": "Accounting Specialist",
      "description": "Accounting Specialist Salary $38,000.00 - $44,000.00 Annually Location 4205 Ryan St, Lake Charles, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number MSU100826U99864 Division Business Affairs Opening Date 10/08/2026 Description Benefits Position/Application Information McNeese State University invites qualified applicants to apply for the position of Accounting Specialist in the McNeese Team Store. This is a full-time, 12-month, unclassified position. The appointment is available October 19, 2026. Position Number: U99864 SALARY: $38,000-$44,000 p/year, commensurate with education and experience POSITION SUMMARY: The Accounting Specialist is responsible for processing, reconciling, documenting, and reporting financial activity for the McNeese Team Store and supporting financial operations for the University Post Office. The position performs accounting support functions related to cash handling, sales reconciliation, purchasing, inventory reporting, departmental billing, and month-end financial activities. The incumbent maintains financial records, prepares reports, and assists management in ensuring the accuracy and completeness of financial transactions in accordance with university policies and procedures. DEADLINE: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until filled. APPLICATION PROCESS AND MATERIALS: Applicants MUST complete an electronic application and upload the required documents listed below: Letter of Application Resume Three (3) References (Include: name and contact information) Unofficial Transcripts *O nly completed application packets including all items listed above will be reviewed. ALL JOB OFFERS ARE CONTINGENT UPON THE SUCCESSFUL RESULT OF A CRIMINAL BACKGROUND CHECK AND RECEIPT OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT(S) IF APPLICABLE. TO APPLY FOR THIS VACANCY, click on the “APPLY” button at the top of advertisement to complete the electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future job opportunities. Applicants are responsible for checking the status of their application to determine where they are in the recruitment process. Further status message information is located under the Information section of the Current Job Opportunities page. * Required application materials WILL NOT be accepted after the deadline, if applicable. Applications may be rejected if incomplete.* CONTACT INFORMATION : IF YOU HAVE QUESTIONS REGARDING THIS POSITION, PLEASE CONTACT THE CHAIR: Tracey Pearce at tpearce@mcneese.edu Office of Human Resources: Kim Dronett, HR Analyst / Recruitment Liaison at kdronett@mcneese.edu . Position Duties/Responsibilities The Accounting Specialist reports to the Team Store Director. Duties and responsibilities include: Financial Operations and Accounting Support Prepare daily sales reconciliations and supporting documentation for Team Store operations, including retail locations, athletic venues, and online sales channels, for management review. Prepare daily cash deposits, cash bags, and related documentation in accordance with established cash handling procedures and internal controls. Process and reconcile payments received through cash, credit card, and electronic payment methods. Prepare purchase orders and maintain receiving documentation in accordance with university purchasing procedures. Maintain and reconcile mobile credit card processing equipment and related transaction reports. Prepare departmental invoices and maintain related billing records. Process and reconcile daily Point-of-Sale transactions and prepare athlete, departmental, and operational reports as required. Research and reconcile outstanding invoices, vendor credits, and customer account discrepancies, reporting issues to management as appropriate. Maintain financial records related to vending operations and prepare associated reports and documentation. Assist the University Post Office Supervisor with Pitney Bowes accounting activities, reconciliations, and reporting requirements. Process Team Store website sales transactions and maintain supporting payment, order, and shipping documentation. Maintain website product information and assist with the uploading and management of inventory images and related content. Financial Reporting and Record Maintenance Prepare and maintain spreadsheets, reports, and supporting documentation related to departmental expenditures, account balances, budget activity, and operational metrics. Generate recurring financial reports, including sales activity, average transaction data, purchasing activity, and other management reports as requested. Review financial transactions and supporting documentation for accuracy and completeness and report discrepancies to the Team Store Manager. Maintain financial records and supporting documentation in accordance with university policies and record retention requirements. Assist Administrative Accounting by preparing reports and supporting documentation required for audits, reconciliations, and financial reporting processes. Month-End, Year-End, and Inventory Reconciliation Perform monthly vendor reconciliations and prepare supporting reports for management review. Prepare monthly sales reconciliations and associated financial reports. Assist with month-end and fiscal year-end closing activities related to sales, inventory, purchasing, and financial records. Prepare textbook buyback, textbook rental, and merchandise reconciliation reports. Maintain inventory-related records and assist with inventory reconciliations, documentation, and reporting activities. Prepare reconciliation schedules and supporting documentation to ensure the completeness and accuracy of financial records. Operations Support and Customer Service Assist with training new employees and student workers on cashiering procedures, financial processes, and Team Store operations. Assist customers, departments, and campus constituents with Team Store transactions and account-related inquiries. Assist with opening PTA accounts and maintaining related customer records and documentation. Support sales floor operations, merchandising activities, and customer service initiatives as needed. Serve as a key-carrying employee and open or close the Team Store as assigned. Perform other duties as assigned in support of Team Store and University Post Office operations. Required/Preferred Qualifications Education Associate or Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a related field preferred. Equivalent combination of education, training, and experience may be considered. Experience Minimum three years of experience in accounting, bookkeeping, financial operations, auditing, cash management, or a closely related field. Experience performing account reconciliations, financial reporting, and cash handling functions preferred. Retail, banking, higher education, or business operations experience preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong knowledge of accounting principles, bookkeeping practices, and financial recordkeeping procedures. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel and other financial software applications. Excellent attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Ability to prepare and reconcile financial reports and supporting documentation. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment when handling financial information. Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff, vendors, and customers. Ability to work independently while managing multiple priorities and deadlines. Knowledge of applicable university policies and procedures, as well as relevant state and federal regulations. General University information McNeese State University, located in Lake Charles, Louisiana, is a public university and a member of the University of Louisiana System. Under Louisiana law, applications and all supporting materials will become public record. All applicants are expected to submit complete and accurate materials as specified in the position announcement. A background check and an English Proficiency assessment (Faculty Only) will be conducted on selected finalists. We comply with Louisiana Revised Statute 49:1001, et seq, and State of Louisiana Executive Order 98-38, which provides for drug testing of employees, appointees, prospective employees, and prospective appointees. Prospective employees and employees are informed if a drug test is required. McNeese State University is an AA/EEO/ADA employer committed to excellence through diversity and a SAME agency (State as a Model Employer for People with Disabilities) for the State of Louisiana. Persons needing reasonable accommodations as provided by the Americans with Disabilities Act should contact the ADA Coordinator, Dr. Desmond Wallace, Office of Inclusive Excellence: Voice: (337) 475-5428; TDD/TTY, Hearing Impaired: (337) 562-4227; or dwallace@mcneese.edu . The Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 requires McNeese State University to inform applicants that the University can employ only U.S. citizens and aliens lawfully authorized to work in the U.S. Each new employee is required to present documentation verifying his/her identity and right to accept employment. McNeese participates in E-Verify. Louisiana Revised Statute 42:31-“Eligibility requirements for certain unclassified employees”-requires any person hired or employed in an unclassified position, whose annual salary or rate of compensation is equal to or exceeds one hundred thousand dollars, provide proof to his public employer that he has been issued a Louisiana driver’s license and that all vehicles registered in his name are registered in Louisiana within thirty days of being hired or employed at such salary. Transcripts from Foreign Universities: Prospective faculty submitting transcripts from foreign universities or schools must have the coursework evaluated for equivalency to United States-accredited coursework by a university-approved agency. The prospective faculty member is responsible for the cost of the evaluation. McNeese typically accepts evaluations by World Education Services (www.wes.org) or Educational Credential Evaluators, Inc.www.ece.org. McNeese State University offers a wide array of benefits to eligible employees to include: Comprehensive retirement programs through the State of Louisiana or Optional program, Supplemental retirement accounts (403B and 457) pre-tax and Roth versions, Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurance to include Vision, Life, Dental, Cancer, Intensive Care, Short Term Disability and more, Paid holidays, Tuition fee reduction program for eligible employees and dependents, Leave accrual and carryover, and many other on campus perks/discount programs. You may view the current year's Benefits Guide at: MYMCNEESE EMPLOYEE EXTRAS Employer McNeese State University Address McNeese State University Box 91615 Lake Charles, Louisiana, 70605 Phone (337) 475-5413 Website https://governmentjobs.com/careers/mcneese Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mcneese/jobs/5378444/assistant-professor-of-accounting": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Accounting Salary $120,000.00 Annually Location 4205 Ryan St, Lake Charles, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number MSU061526F99595 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 06/16/2026 Description Benefits Position/Application Information McNeese State University invites qualified applicants and nominations for the position of Assistant Professor of Accounting in the Department of Business Disciplines. This is a full-time, unclassified, 9-month, tenure-track position. The appointment begins in January 2027. Position Number:F99595 SALARY: $120,000 (non-negotiable) COLLEGE: The College of Business programs are accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business International (AACSB). The College currently offers a BS in Business Administration with majors in Accounting, Business Administration, Finance, Management, and Marketing; an MBA; and an undergraduate certificate in LNG Business. DEADLINE: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until filled. APPLICATION PROCESS AND MATERIALS: Applicants MUST complete an electronic application and upload the required documents listed below: Letter of Application with description of experience relevant to the position Current CV Teaching Evaluations Sample of Research Three References (names and contact information) Unofficial Transcripts *O nly completed application packets including all items listed above will be reviewed. ALL JOB OFFERS ARE CONTINGENT UPON THE SUCCESSFUL RESULT OF A CRIMINAL BACKGROUND CHECK AND RECEIPT OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT(S) IF APPLICABLE. TO APPLY FOR THIS VACANCY, click on the “APPLY” button at the top of advertisement to complete the electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future job opportunities. Applicants are responsible for checking the status of their application to determine where they are in the recruitment process. Further status message information is located under the Information section of the Current Job Opportunities page. * Required application materials WILL NOT be accepted after the deadline, if applicable. Applications may be rejected if incomplete.* IF YOU HAVE QUESTIONS REGARDING THIS POSITION, PLEASE CONTACT THE CHAIR: Daryl Burckel at dburckel@mcneese.edu Office of Human Resources: Kim Dronett, HR Analyst/Recruitment kdronett@mcneese.edu or (337) 475-5413 Position Duties/Responsibilities The Assistant Professor is responsible for excellent teaching, a commitment to intellectual contributions, and service to the profession and the university. The candidate must have outstanding teaching through classroom engagement and participation in a face-to-face environment. The candidate also needs to be proficient in online teaching. Teaching duties will include but are not limited to Intermediate I, Intermediate II, Accounting Theory, and Advanced Accounting. Advising students is also required. The candidate must contribute intellectually through publications in quality journals (as specified in ABDC and SJR) and collaborate with their fellow peers. A successful candidate must meet the College of Business criteria for Scholarly Academic (SA) status in accordance with AACSB standards. For the service component, the candidate will serve on committees at both the college and university level, be actively involved in college recruitment and the profession. Required/Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates possessing a terminal degree in accounting or related discipline. The successful candidate’s research record should be in compliance with AACSB-International’s standard on faculty qualifications. Applicants must hold SA status (Scholarly Academic) by the job start date. The successful candidate should demonstrate excellence in teaching, a commitment to intellectual contributions, and a desire to provide service to the university and the profession. General University information McNeese State University, located in Lake Charles, Louisiana, is a public university and a member of the University of Louisiana System. Under Louisiana law, applications and all supporting materials will become public record. All applicants are expected to submit complete and accurate materials as specified in the position announcement. A background check and an English Proficiency assessment (Faculty Only) will be conducted on selected finalists. We comply with Louisiana Revised Statute 49:1001, et seq, and State of Louisiana Executive Order 98-38, which provides for drug testing of employees, appointees, prospective employees, and prospective appointees. Prospective employees and employees are informed if a drug test is required. McNeese State University is an AA/EEO/ADA employer committed to excellence through diversity and a SAME agency (State as a Model Employer for People with Disabilities) for the State of Louisiana. Persons needing reasonable accommodations as provided by the Americans with Disabilities Act should contact the ADA Coordinator, Krisshunn Youngblood, Office of Inclusive Excellence: Voice: (337) 475-5428; TDD/TTY, Hearing Impaired: (337) 562-4227; or kyoungblood@mcneese.edu . The Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 requires McNeese State University to inform applicants that the University can employ only U.S. citizens and aliens lawfully authorized to work in the U.S. Each new employee is required to present documentation verifying his/her identity and right to accept employment. McNeese participates in E-Verify. Louisiana Revised Statute 42:31-“Eligibility requirements for certain unclassified employees”-requires any person hired or employed in an unclassified position, whose annual salary or rate of compensation is equal to or exceeds one hundred thousand dollars, provide proof to his public employer that he has been issued a Louisiana driver’s license and that all vehicles registered in his name are registered in Louisiana within thirty days of being hired or employed at such salary. Transcripts from Foreign Universities: Prospective faculty submitting transcripts from foreign universities or schools must have the coursework evaluated for equivalency to United States-accredited coursework by a University-approved agency. The prospective faculty member is responsible for the cost of the evaluation. McNeese typically accepts evaluations by World Education Services ( www.wes.org ) or Educational Credential Evaluators, Inc. www.ece.org . McNeese State University offers a wide array of benefits to eligible employees to include: Comprehensive retirement programs through the State of Louisiana or Optional program, Supplemental retirement accounts (403B and 457) pre-tax and Roth versions, Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurance to include Vision, Life, Dental, Cancer, Intensive Care, Short Term Disability and more, Paid holidays, Tuition fee reduction program for eligible employees and dependents, Leave accrual and carryover, and many other on campus perks/discount programs. You may view the current year's Benefits Guide at: MYMCNEESE EMPLOYEE EXTRAS Employer McNeese State University Address McNeese State University Box 91615 Lake Charles, Louisiana, 70605 Phone (337) 475-5413 Website https://governmentjobs.com/careers/mcneese Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mcneese/jobs/5477363/assistant-professor-of-biology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Biology Salary $55,000.00 Annually Location 4205 Ryan St, Lake Charles, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number MSU090926F99967 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 09/09/2026 Description Benefits Position/Application Information The Department of Biology at McNeese State University is accepting applicants for the position of Assistant Professor of Biology. This is a full-time, 9-month, unclassified, tenure-track position. The appointment begins in August 2027. Position Number: F99967 SALARY: $55,000 DEADLINE: Review of applications will begin October 20, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. APPLICATION PROCESS AND MATERIALS: For the application process, applicants MUST complete an electronic application and upload required documents listed below to ensure full consideration: Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Philosophy Three References (include: name, phone number, and email address) Unofficial Transcripts for all degrees earned Note : Three letters of recommendation will be required at time of hire on selected candidate . *O nly completed application packets including all items listed above will be reviewed. ALL JOB OFFERS ARE CONTINGENT UPON THE SUCCESSFUL RESULT OF A CRIMINAL BACKGROUND CHECK AND RECEIPT OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT(S) IF APPLICABLE. TO APPLY FOR THIS VACANCY, click on the “APPLY” button at the top of advertisement to complete the electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future job opportunities. Applicants are responsible for checking the status of their application to determine where they are in the recruitment process. Further status message information is located under the Information section of the Current Job Opportunities page. * Required application materials WILL NOT be accepted after the deadline, if applicable. Applications may be rejected if incomplete. * CONTACT INFORMATION: QUESTIONS REGARDING THIS POSITION MAY BE DIRECTED TO THE CHAIR: Dr. Sarah Baker at sbaker17@mcneese.edu or Phone: (337) 475-5665 Office of Human Resources Contact: Kim Dronett, HR Analyst/Recruitment Liaison at kdronett@mcneese.edu or (337) 475-5413 Position Duties/Responsibilities The successful candidate will be responsible for functions related to teaching, advising, research, and service. We are seeking a broadly trained ecologist, wildlife/fisheries biologist, or natural resource biologist that can teach courses in one or more of the following areas: ecology of wetlands, wildlife population dynamics, wildlife techniques, game management. The successful candidate also will be provided with opportunities to develop and teach advanced undergraduate/graduate courses in their area of specialty. Standard teaching responsibility will be 12 contact hours per regular semester and may include evenings. Summer teaching may also be available. The successful candidate is expected to develop an active research program in their field of expertise, recruit and mentor graduate/undergraduate students, present their research at professional meetings, and publish their findings in peer-reviewed journals. Required/Preferred Qualifications Required : Earned doctorate in biology, wildlife/fisheries management, natural resource management, or related area and excellent written and oral communication skills. General University information McNeese State University, located in Lake Charles, Louisiana, is a public university and a member of the University of Louisiana System. Under Louisiana law, applications and all supporting materials will become public record. All applicants are expected to submit complete and accurate materials as specified in the position announcement. A background check and an English Proficiency assessment (Faculty Only) will be conducted on selected finalists. We comply with Louisiana Revised Statute 49:1001, et seq, and State of Louisiana Executive Order 98-38, which provides for drug testing of employees, appointees, prospective employees, and prospective appointees. Prospective employees and employees are informed if a drug test is required. McNeese State University is an AA/EEO/ADA employer committed to excellence through diversity and a SAME agency (State as a Model Employer for People with Disabilities) for the State of Louisiana. Persons requesting accommodations in accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) should contact the Office of Campus Compliance and Civility at least 72 hours before the event. Additional information is available from the Office of Campus Compliance and Civility, located in the Burton Business Center, Suite 407, by phone at 337-475-5428, by fax at 337-475-5603, or by email at compliance@mcneese.edu . The Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 requires McNeese State University to inform applicants that the University can employ only U.S. citizens and aliens lawfully authorized to work in the U.S. Each new employee is required to present documentation verifying his/her identity and right to accept employment. McNeese participates in E-Verify. Louisiana Revised Statute 42:31-“Eligibility requirements for certain unclassified employees”-requires any person hired or employed in an unclassified position, whose annual salary or rate of compensation is equal to or exceeds one hundred thousand dollars, provide proof to his public employer that he has been issued a Louisiana driver’s license and that all vehicles registered in his name are registered in Louisiana within thirty days of being hired or employed at such salary. Transcripts from Foreign Universities: Prospective faculty submitting transcripts from foreign universities or schools must have the coursework evaluated for equivalency to United States-accredited coursework by a University-approved agency. The prospective faculty member is responsible for the cost of the evaluation. McNeese typically accepts evaluations by World Education Services ( www.wes.org ) or Educational Credential Evaluators, Inc. www.ece.org . McNeese State University offers a wide array of benefits to eligible employees to include: Comprehensive retirement programs through the State of Louisiana or Optional program, Supplemental retirement accounts (403B and 457) pre-tax and Roth versions, Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurance to include Vision, Life, Dental, Cancer, Intensive Care, Short Term Disability and more, Paid holidays, Tuition fee reduction program for eligible employees and dependents, Leave accrual and carryover, and many other on campus perks/discount programs. You may view the current year's Benefits Guide at: MYMCNEESE EMPLOYEE EXTRAS Employer McNeese State University Address McNeese State University Box 91615 Lake Charles, Louisiana, 70605 Phone (337) 475-5413 Website https://governmentjobs.com/careers/mcneese Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mcneese/jobs/5469301/assistant-professor-of-civil-engineering": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Civil Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Civil Engineering Salary $76,000.00 Annually Location 4205 Ryan St, Lake Charles, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number MSU090126F99680 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 09/01/2026 Description Benefits Position/Application Information McNeese State University invites applicants for the position of Assistant Professor of Civil Engineering in the Department of Engineering and Computer Science. Applications are welcomed from all areas of civil engineering, with particular interest in water resources and hydraulic engineering, structural engineering, geotechnical engineering, transportation engineering, materials engineering, and environmental engineering. This is a full-time, 9-month, unclassified, tenure-track position. The appointment will begin in spring, January 2027. Position Number: F99680 SALARY: $76,000 DEADLINE: Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain open until position is filled. APPLICATION PROCESS AND MATERIALS: For the application process, applicants MUST complete an electronic application and upload required documents listed below: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Three Professional References (Include: name, phone number, and email address) Unofficial Transcripts for all degrees earned Cover Letter O nly completed application packets including all items listed above will be reviewed. ALL JOB OFFERS ARE CONTINGENT UPON THE SUCCESSFUL RESULT OF A CRIMINAL BACKGROUND CHECK AND RECEIPT OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT(S) IF APPLICABLE. TO APPLY FOR THIS VACANCY, click on the “APPLY” button at the top of advertisement to complete the electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future job opportunities. Applicants are responsible for checking the status of their application to determine where they are in the recruitment process. Further status message information is located under the Information section of the Current Job Opportunities page. * Required application materials WILL NOT be accepted after the deadline, if applicable. Applications may be rejected if incomplete. CONTACT INFORMATION: QUESTIONS REGARDING THIS POSITION MAY BE DIRECTED TO THE CHAIR: Dr. Ning Zhang, Dept. Head of Engineering & Computer Science at nzhang@mcneese.edu Office of Human Resources Contact: Kim Dronett, HR Analyst/Recruitment at kdronett@mcneese.edu or (337) 475-5413 Position Duties/Responsibilities The Assistant Professor is responsible for functions related to teaching courses, advising students, and conducting research. The assistant professor will work closely with faculty and staff in the Department of Engineering and Computer Science. Required/Preferred Qualifications Required : PhD in Civil Engineering Preferred : Experience in Civil Engineering and related field General University information McNeese State University, located in Lake Charles, Louisiana, is a public university and a member of the University of Louisiana System. Under Louisiana law, applications and all supporting materials will become public record. All applicants are expected to submit complete and accurate materials as specified in the position announcement. A background check and an English Proficiency assessment (Faculty Only) will be conducted on selected finalists. We comply with Louisiana Revised Statute 49:1001, et seq, and State of Louisiana Executive Order 98-38, which provides for drug testing of employees, appointees, prospective employees, and prospective appointees. Prospective employees and employees are informed if a drug test is required. McNeese State University is an AA/EEO/ADA employer committed to excellence through diversity and a SAME agency (State as a Model Employer for People with Disabilities) for the State of Louisiana. Persons requesting accommodations in accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) should contact the Office of Campus Compliance and Civility at least 72 hours before the event. Additional information is available from the Office of Campus Compliance and Civility, located in the Burton Business Center, Suite 407, by phone at 337-475-5428, by fax at 337-475-5603, or by email at compliance@mcneese.edu . The Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 requires McNeese State University to inform applicants that the University can employ only U.S. citizens and aliens lawfully authorized to work in the U.S. Each new employee is required to present documentation verifying his/her identity and right to accept employment. McNeese participates in E-Verify. Louisiana Revised Statute 42:31-“Eligibility requirements for certain unclassified employees”-requires any person hired or employed in an unclassified position, whose annual salary or rate of compensation is equal to or exceeds one hundred thousand dollars, provide proof to his public employer that he has been issued a Louisiana driver’s license and that all vehicles registered in his name are registered in Louisiana within thirty days of being hired or employed at such salary. Transcripts from Foreign Universities: Prospective faculty submitting transcripts from foreign universities or schools must have the coursework evaluated for equivalency to United States-accredited coursework by a University-approved agency. The prospective faculty member is responsible for the cost of the evaluation. McNeese typically accepts evaluations by World Education Services ( www.wes.org ) or Educational Credential Evaluators, Inc www.wes.org . McNeese State University offers a wide array of benefits to eligible employees to include: Comprehensive retirement programs through the State of Louisiana or Optional program, Supplemental retirement accounts (403B and 457) pre-tax and Roth versions, Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurance to include Vision, Life, Dental, Cancer, Intensive Care, Short Term Disability and more, Paid holidays, Tuition fee reduction program for eligible employees and dependents, Leave accrual and carryover, and many other on campus perks/discount programs. You may view the current year's Benefits Guide at: MYMCNEESE EMPLOYEE EXTRAS Employer McNeese State University Address McNeese State University Box 91615 Lake Charles, Louisiana, 70605 Phone (337) 475-5413 Website https://governmentjobs.com/careers/mcneese Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mcneese/jobs/5503211/assistant-professor-of-kinesiology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Kinesiology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Kinesiology Salary $55,000.00 Annually Location 4205 Ryan St, Lake Charles, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number MSU100226F99682 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 10/02/2026 Description Benefits Position/Application Information McNeese State University invites qualified applicants for the position of Assistant Professor of Kinesiology in the H.C. Drew School of Kinesiology in the Burton College of Education. This is a full time, 9-month, unclassified tenure-track position. The appointment is available August (Fall) 2027 semester. Position Number: F99682 Salary: $55,000 Deadline: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until position is filled. APPLICATION PROCESS AND MATERIALS: For the application process, applicants MUST complete an electronic application and upload required documents listed below: Letter of Application with relevance to the position CV Three References (Include: name, phone number, and email address) Unofficial Transcripts O nly completed application packets including all items listed above will be reviewed. ALL JOB OFFERS ARE CONTINGENT UPON THE SUCCESSFUL RESULT OF A CRIMINAL BACKGROUND CHECK AND RECEIPT OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT(S) IF APPLICABLE. TO APPLY FOR THIS VACANCY, click on the “APPLY” button at the top of advertisement to complete the electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future job opportunities. Applicants are responsible for checking the status of their application to determine where they are in the recruitment process. Further status message information is located under the Information section of the Current Job Opportunities page. * Required application materials WILL NOT be accepted after the deadline, if applicable. Applications may be rejected if incomplete. CONTACT INFORMATION : IF YOU HAVE QUESTIONS REGARDING THIS POSITION, PLEASE CONTACT: Dr. Staci Henry, Search Committee Chair at shenry@mcneese.edu OR Carroll Patin, Department Head at cpatin@mcneese.edu Office of Human Resources Contact: Kim Dronett, HR Analyst/Recruitment kdronett@mcneese.edu or (337) 475-5413 Position Duties/Responsibilities The Assistant Professor of Kinesiology is responsible for teaching 12 credit hours of undergraduate and graduate courses that prepare students for careers in exercise physiology, sport management, strength and conditioning, and related allied health professions. This faculty member will collaborate with colleagues, students, and community partners to support high-quality teaching, scholarship, and service. Responsibilities include advising undergraduate and graduate students across two to four concentrations within the Department of Kinesiology; serving on departmental, college, and university committees; and actively participating in student recruitment activities throughout the academic year. The Assistant Professor is also expected to engage in ongoing professional development to maintain current knowledge and expertise in the discipline, regardless of certification or licensure status. Required/Preferred Qualifications Required : Earned doctorate or terminal degree in Kinesiology or closely related field. Evidence of effective teaching or teaching potential at the collegiate level. Ability to recruit, retain, and advise undergraduate and/or graduate students. Demonstrated commitment to working collaboratively with colleagues, staff, students, and/or community partners. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to scholarly activity and professional development. Preferred : Higher education teaching experience. Current professional certifications relevant to the discipline. Record of scholarly publications, presentations, or externally funded research. Experience using learning management systems (e.g. Canvas) and instructional technology. Experience in collaborating with schools, healthcare organizations, athletic organizations, or community partners. Experience with operating and/or managing an Exercise Science or Human Performance Laboratory, Note : Applicants who do not hold a terminal degree but possess a master's degree in a related field may be considered for appointment at the rank of Instructor in a non-tenure-track, nine-month position with a lower salary. McNeese State University offers a wide array of benefits to eligible employees to include: Comprehensive retirement programs through the State of Louisiana or Optional program, Supplemental retirement accounts (403B and 457) pre-tax and Roth versions, Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurance to include Vision, Life, Dental, Cancer, Intensive Care, Short Term Disability and more, Paid holidays, Tuition fee reduction program for eligible employees and dependents, Leave accrual and carryover, and many other on campus perks/discount programs. You may view the current year's Benefits Guide at: MYMCNEESE EMPLOYEE EXTRAS Employer McNeese State University Address McNeese State University Box 91615 Lake Charles, Louisiana, 70605 Phone (337) 475-5413 Website https://governmentjobs.com/careers/mcneese Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mcneese/jobs/5394817/assistant-professor-of-psychology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Psychology Salary $60,000.00 Annually Location 4205 Ryan St, Lake Charles, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number MSU063026F99679 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 06/30/2026 Description Benefits Position/Application Information McNeese State University invites applicants to apply for the position of Assistant Professor of Psychology in the Department of Psychology and Counseling, in the College of Nursing and Health Professions. Our faculty seeks enthusiastic candidates who share our commitment to ensuring that McNeese State University is the first choice for students seeking to study psychology. This is an in-person, full-time, 9–month, tenure-track, unclassified position. The on-campus appointment will begin in August (Fall) 2026. Position Number: F99679 Job Perks : Opportunities for salary supplement through paid summer teaching available upon request. Excellent fringe benefits including tuition reduction for employee, spouse, and dependent children; excellent healthcare benefits; and reimbursement for professional development needs such as CEUs towards any credentialing and conference travel. SALARY: $60,000 DEPARTMENT/COLLEGE: The Department of Psychology and Counseling at McNeese State University seeks to hire one full-time tenure-track faculty member in its B.S. in Psychology degree program. The successful candidate will join undergraduate and graduate faculty in its 10-member department housed in the College of Nursing and Health Professions. Faculty often receive financial support for research and teaching initiatives through the college and university endowed professor funds and technology enhancement awards. Conference travel is encouraged and supported by Departmental funding. Our program is enthusiastic about teaching and student research with a focus on the three-course undergraduate research sequence. Students receive the foundational underpinnings of conducting research, develop a research question, submit an HSIRB application, and collect and analyze data. The three courses culminate in a public poster defense and an APA paper of their research. Faculty enjoy flexible schedules that include both face-to-face instruction and online teaching along with optional paid summer teaching opportunities. The ideal candidates will also value teaching, evidence-based practice, and have research experience. Our current faculty have diverse backgrounds in behavior analysis/behavior science, cognitive science, counselor education, experimental psychology, and special education. Please consider joining our department. ABD candidates will also be happily considered. Additional information about the Department of Psychology and Counseling can be viewed at www.mcneese.edu/nursing/psychology . Additional information about McNeese State University can be viewed at https://www.mcneese.edu/ . DEADLINE: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until position is filled. APPLICATION PROCESS AND MATERIALS: Applicants MUST complete an electronic application and upload the required documents listed below: Letter of Application (Cover Letter) Vita Names and contact information for 3 references (include: name, phone number, and email address) Unofficial Transcripts for all degrees earned* Finalists will be asked to submit a brief teaching sample* * Note : Official Transcripts and Three Letters of Recommendation will be required at time of hire of the selected candidate. Only completed application packets including all items listed above will be reviewed. ALL JOB OFFERS ARE CONTINGENT UPON THE SUCCESSFUL RESULT OF A CRIMINAL BACKGROUND CHECK AND RECEIPT OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT(S) IF APPLICABLE. TO APPLY FOR THIS VACANCY, click on the “APPLY” button at the top of advertisement to complete the electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future job opportunities. Applicants are responsible for checking the status of their application to determine where they are in the recruitment process. Further status message information is located under the Information section of the Current Job Opportunities page. CONTACT INFORMATION : QUESTIONS REGARDING THIS POSITION MAY BE DIRECTED TO THE CHAIR: Joanna Thompson, PhD, BCBA-D at jthompson2@mcneese.edu Office of Human Resources: Kim Dronett, HR Analyst/Recruitment at kdronett@mcneese.edu or (337) 475-5413 Position Duties/Responsibilities Responsibilities will include but are not limited to: teaching psychology at the undergraduate level; teaching undergraduate research from study design to implementation to public presentation; university and community service, advising; modeling ethical behavior; and research/scholarship. Assistant Professors will work closely with students and faculty in the Department of Psychology and Counseling. Primary duties are centered around teaching and involvement in our undergraduate research sequence. Successful candidates are expected to behave in accordance with the overall mission and philosophy of our University and department. Required/Preferred Qualifications Minimum Required : Doctorate in psychology or experimental psychology or a closely related discipline Strong background in research Evidence of effective teaching of research at the undergraduate level Preferred: Working knowledge of Microsoft excel as well as online software for conducting statistical analyses Experience with helping students develop research ideas, write research proposals, and complete IRB applications History of collaborative research with other faculty, colleagues, and/or students, leading to conference presentations and/or publications Experience with tracking or supervising online research sessions and data management systems Experience working with or on an IRB committee General University information McNeese State University, located in Lake Charles, Louisiana, is a public university and a member of the University of Louisiana System. Under Louisiana law, applications and all supporting materials will become public record. All applicants are expected to submit complete and accurate materials as specified in the position announcement. A background check and an English Proficiency assessment (Faculty Only) will be conducted on selected finalists. We comply with Louisiana Revised Statute 49:1001, et seq, and State of Louisiana Executive Order 98-38, which provides for drug testing of employees, appointees, prospective employees, and prospective appointees. Prospective employees and employees are informed if a drug test is required. McNeese State University is an AA/EEO/ADA employer committed to excellence through diversity and a SAME agency (State as a Model Employer for People with Disabilities) for the State of Louisiana. Persons requesting accommodations in accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) should contact the Office of Campus Compliance and Civility at least 72 hours before the event. Additional information is available from the Office of Campus Compliance and Civility, located in the Burton Business Center, Suite 407, by phone at 337-475-5428, by fax at 337-475-5603, or by email at compliance@mcneese.edu . The Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 requires McNeese State University to inform applicants that the University can employ only U.S. citizens and aliens lawfully authorized to work in the U.S. Each new employee is required to present documentation verifying his/her identity and right to accept employment. McNeese participates in E-Verify. Louisiana Revised Statute 42:31-“Eligibility requirements for certain unclassified employees”-requires any person hired or employed in an unclassified position, whose annual salary or rate of compensation is equal to or exceeds one hundred thousand dollars, provide proof to his public employer that he has been issued a Louisiana driver’s license and that all vehicles registered in his name are registered in Louisiana within thirty days of being hired or employed at such salary. Transcripts from Foreign Universities: Prospective faculty submitting transcripts from foreign universities or schools must have the coursework evaluated for equivalency to United States-accredited coursework by a University-approved agency. The prospective faculty member is responsible for the cost of the evaluation. McNeese typically accepts evaluations by World Education Services ( www.wes.org ) or Educational Credential Evaluators, Inc. www.ece.org . McNeese State University offers a wide array of benefits to eligible employees to include: Comprehensive retirement programs through the State of Louisiana or Optional program, Supplemental retirement accounts (403B and 457) pre-tax and Roth versions, Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurance to include Vision, Life, Dental, Cancer, Intensive Care, Short Term Disability and more, Paid holidays, Tuition fee reduction program for eligible employees and dependents, Leave accrual and carryover, and many other on campus perks/discount programs. You may view the current year's Benefits Guide at: MYMCNEESE EMPLOYEE EXTRAS Employer McNeese State University Address McNeese State University Box 91615 Lake Charles, Louisiana, 70605 Phone (337) 475-5413 Website https://governmentjobs.com/careers/mcneese Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mcneese/jobs/5488698/associate-director-of-recreation-and-wellness-programs": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Recreation and Wellness Programs",
      "description": "Associate Director of Recreation and Wellness Programs Salary $48,000.00 - $54,000.00 Annually Location 4205 Ryan St, Lake Charles, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number MSU091826U99475 Division Student Affairs Opening Date 09/19/2026 Description Benefits Position/Application Information McNeese State University invites applicants for the position of Associate Director of Recreation and Wellness Programs. This is a full-time, 12-month, unclassified staff position. This appointment is available to begin October 1, 2026. Position Number: U99475 SALARY: $48,000 - $54,000 per year, pending education and experience DEADLINE: Position will remain open until filled. APPLICATION PROCESS AND MATERIALS: For the application process, applicants MUST complete an electronic application and upload required documents listed below: Letter of application (cover letter) Resume Unofficial transcripts Three (3) professional references (Include: name, phone number, and e-mail address) O nly completed application packets including all items listed above will be reviewed. ALL JOB OFFERS ARE CONTINGENT UPON THE SUCCESSFUL RESULT OF A CRIMINAL BACKGROUND CHECK AND RECEIPT OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT(S) IF APPLICABLE. TO APPLY FOR THIS VACANCY, click on the “APPLY” button at the top of advertisement to complete the electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future job opportunities. Applicants are responsible for checking the status of their application to determine where they are in the recruitment process. Further status message information is located under the Information section of the Current Job Opportunities page. * Required application materials WILL NOT be accepted after the deadline, if applicable. Applications may be rejected if incomplete. CONTACT INFORMATION: QUESTIONS REGARDING THIS POSITION MAY BE DIRECTED TO THE CHAIR: Jordan Owens at jowens11@mcneese.edu Office of Human Resources Contact : Kim Dronett, HR Analyst/Employment Liaison: kdronett@mcneese.edu or (337) 475-5413 Position Duties/Responsibilities The Associate Director of Recreation and Wellness Programs is an employee within Recreation and Wellness Programs. The position reports to the Director of Recreation Complex and Wellness Programs. The Associate Director is responsible for the following job functions: Develop and administer a program of informal recreation activities designed to meet the needs of a diverse campus community Assist with developing and implementing marketing and promotional plans for the recreation complex, including recreation and wellness programs and initiatives Assist in managing all recreational facilities Interview, hire, train, schedule, supervise, and keep time records of all student personnel Ensure facility equipment meets the highest standards for safety and operational effectiveness Conduct periodic inspections of all recreation complex equipment and make or coordinate needed repairs; contact appropriate vendors for equipment repair and/or replacement Conduct or oversee preventative maintenance on equipment at regular intervals Assist in inspecting facility for cleanliness and coordinate appropriate services as needed Contribute to the long-term planning and execution of minor planned projects including capital renovation and construction projects; serve as project manager as needed Assist with communication with the Office of Facilities and Plant Operations and Custodial Services concerning maintenance/custodial needs for the recreation complex Assist in developing educational materials for current and potential members Assist with risk management policies and procedures Assist with daily deposit procedures for the rec complex Develop and evaluate informal recreation programs and student personnel Work cooperatively with the Director of Recreation and Wellness Programs to execute intramural sports when assigned Maintain a current inventory of all equipment and supplies Lead the development, implementation, and evaluation of wellness programming and initiatives designed to promote health, fitness, and overall well-being among the campus community Coordinate and schedule group fitness classes, wellness classes, instructors, facilities, and related program logistics Develop, coordinate, and execute wellness programming events and activities throughout the academic year Identify opportunities to expand wellness programming based on student needs, participation trends, and campus interests Coordinate wellness initiatives and partnerships with campus departments, student organizations, and external partners Assist with monitoring expenses and revenue goals, and identify opportunities for revenue and grants to support operations and facility improvements, such as the Technology Assessment Student Committee (TASC) or Campus Development Committee (CDC) Assist with cultivating partnerships with internal and external organizations, contribute to the development and execution of partner agreements, and the scheduling and execution of events Participate in professional development programs Serve as a member of university committees as assigned Provide backup support for urgent and emergency situations involving the recreation complex when the Director is unavailable, particularly during the academic semester Perform other job-related duties as required and assigned by the Director or next-level supervision Required/Preferred Qualifications R equired: Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited institution 2 years of professional experience in recreational sports, physical wellness, facility management, student development, student life, or a similar role Supervision experience of persons 18 years of age or older Evidence of strong communication and interpersonal skills Proficiency using Microsoft Office products and other computer software Ability to work evenings, nights, and weekends as necessary Ability to lift 25 pounds Experience working with diverse populations Evidence of an energetic, student-centered approach to program development and delivery Preferred: Master’s degree in health and human performance, physical education, student services, higher education, or closely related field 3 or more years of professional experience in recreational sports, physical wellness, facility management, student development, student life or a similar role Membership experience in an organization or association relative to higher education, recreational sports, or physical wellness Certification in First Aid/CPR/AED Experience allocating and managing budgets Experience in policy development, enforcement, and compliance monitoring in an educational setting Familiarity with relevant legal issues at the local, state, and federal level Basic working knowledge of sports rules and structure General University information McNeese State University, located in Lake Charles, Louisiana, is a public university and a member of the University of Louisiana System. Under Louisiana law, applications and all supporting materials will become public record. All applicants are expected to submit complete and accurate materials as specified in the position announcement. A background check and an English Proficiency assessment (Faculty Only) will be conducted on selected finalists. We comply with Louisiana Revised Statute 49:1001, et seq, and State of Louisiana Executive Order 98-38, which provides for drug testing of employees, appointees, prospective employees, and prospective appointees. Prospective employees and employees are informed if a drug test is required. McNeese State University is an AA/EEO/ADA employer committed to excellence through diversity and a SAME agency (State as a Model Employer for People with Disabilities) for the State of Louisiana. Persons needing reasonable accommodations as provided by the Americans with Disabilities Act should contact the ADA Coordinator, Dr. Desmond Wallace, Office of Inclusive Excellence: Voice: (337) 475-5428; TDD/TTY, Hearing Impaired: (337) 562-4227; or dwallace@mcneese.edu . The Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 requires McNeese State University to inform applicants that the University can employ only U.S. citizens and aliens lawfully authorized to work in the U.S. Each new employee is required to present documentation verifying his/her identity and right to accept employment. McNeese participates in E-Verify. Louisiana Revised Statute 42:31-“Eligibility requirements for certain unclassified employees”-requires any person hired or employed in an unclassified position, whose annual salary or rate of compensation is equal to or exceeds one hundred thousand dollars, provide proof to his public employer that he has been issued a Louisiana driver’s license and that all vehicles registered in his name are registered in Louisiana within thirty days of being hired or employed at such salary. Transcripts from Foreign Universities: Prospective faculty submitting transcripts from foreign universities or schools must have the coursework evaluated for equivalency to United States-accredited coursework by a university-approved agency. The prospective faculty member is responsible for the cost of the evaluation. McNeese typically accepts evaluations by World Education Services ( www.wes.org ) or Educational Credential Evaluators, Inc. www.ece.org . McNeese State University offers a wide array of benefits to eligible employees to include: Comprehensive retirement programs through the State of Louisiana or Optional program, Supplemental retirement accounts (403B and 457) pre-tax and Roth versions, Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurance to include Vision, Life, Dental, Cancer, Intensive Care, Short Term Disability and more, Paid holidays, Tuition fee reduction program for eligible employees and dependents, Leave accrual and carryover, and many other on campus perks/discount programs. You may view the current year's Benefits Guide at: MYMCNEESE EMPLOYEE EXTRAS Employer McNeese State University Address McNeese State University Box 91615 Lake Charles, Louisiana, 70605 Phone (337) 475-5413 Website https://governmentjobs.com/careers/mcneese Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mcneese/jobs/5412195/clinical-assistant-professor": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor Location 4205 Ryan St, Lake Charles, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number MSU071526F99993-59 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 07/15/2026 Description Benefits Position/Application Information McNeese State University is accepting applications to fill the position for Clinical Assistant Professor of Undergraduate Nursing. Applicants from all clinical backgrounds are welcome to apply. DEPARTMENT: Undergraduate Nursing/ College of Nursing and Health Professions POSITION INFORMATION: This is a full-time, 9-month, unclassified, clinical assistant instructor. The appointment begins in Fall 2026. POSITION NUMBER: F99993 / F99959 SALARY: Commensurate with experience. REPORTING AUTHORITY: Department Head DEADLINE: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. APPLICATION PROCESS AND MATERIALS: For the application process, applicants MUST complete an electronic application and upload required documents listed below: Letter of Application Resume Three Letters of Recommendation Unofficial Transcripts *Only completed application packets including all items listed above will be reviewed. ALL JOB OFFERS ARE CONTINGENT UPON THE SUCCESSFUL RESULT OF A CRIMINAL BACKGROUND CHECK AND RECEIPT OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT(S) IF APPLICABLE. TO APPLY FOR THIS VACANCY, click on the “APPLY” button at the top of advertisement to complete the electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future job opportunities. Applicants are responsible for checking the status of their application to determine where they are in the recruitment process. Further status message information is located under the Information section of the Current Job Opportunities page. *Required application materials WILL NOT be accepted after the deadline, if applicable. Applications may be rejected if incomplete.* CONTACT INFORMATION: QUESTIONS REGARDING THIS POSITION MAY BE DIRECTED TO THE CHAIR: Amelia Washington at awashington2@mcneese.edu Office of Human Resources Contact: Kim Dronett, HR Analyst/Recruitment kdronett@mcneese.edu or (337) 475-5413 Position Duties/Responsibilities The Assistant Professor, a faculty member in the Undergraduate Nursing Degree Program, has responsibilities that include but are not limited to: administration, teaching, university/community service, and research/scholarly work. Specific duties include: implementing University and College policies and procedures; implementing the program curricula; participating in curriculum and course planning, implementation, and evaluation; student advisement; mentoring; assisting in evaluating clinical settings and experiences related to the course and student learning needs; planning clinical experiences for students and evaluating the clinical competence of students; serves on University and College of Nursing committees; participates in the community by offering volunteer services and/or offering consultation and/or in-service education to clinical agencies or community agencies/organizations; and initiates and/or participates in nursing research activities. Required/Preferred Qualifications Required : Bachelor’s and master's degrees in nursing are required. Academic preparation includes degree specialization, specialty coursework, or other preparation sufficient to address the qualifications. At least two years of clinical practice are required in the nursing field of expertise and current, unencumbered licensure in Louisiana. This position requires in-person teaching on campus. Desired : Doctorate in Nursing or related field preferred. General University information McNeese State University, located in Lake Charles, Louisiana, is a public university and a member of the University of Louisiana System. Under Louisiana law, applications and all supporting materials will become public record. All applicants are expected to submit complete and accurate materials as specified in the position announcement. A background check and an English Proficiency assessment (Faculty Only) will be conducted on selected finalists. We comply with Louisiana Revised Statute 49:1001, et seq, and State of Louisiana Executive Order 98-38, which provides for drug testing of employees, appointees, prospective employees, and prospective appointees. Prospective employees and employees are informed if a drug test is required. McNeese State University is an AA/EEO/ADA employer committed to excellence through diversity and a SAME agency (State as a Model Employer for People with Disabilities) for the State of Louisiana. Persons requesting accommodations in accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) should contact the Office of Campus Compliance and Civility at least 72 hours before the event. Additional information is available from the Office of Campus Compliance and Civility, located in the Burton Business Center, Suite 407, by phone at 337-475-5428, by fax at 337-475-5603, or by email at compliance@mcneese.edu .? The Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 requires McNeese State University to inform applicants that the University can employ only U.S. citizens and aliens lawfully authorized to work in the U.S. Each new employee is required to present documentation verifying his/her identity and right to accept employment. McNeese participates in E-Verify. Louisiana Revised Statute 42:31-“Eligibility requirements for certain unclassified employees”-requires any person hired or employed in an unclassified position, whose annual salary or rate of compensation is equal to or exceeds one hundred thousand dollars, provide proof to his public employer that he has been issued a Louisiana driver’s license and that all vehicles registered in his name are registered in Louisiana within thirty days of being hired or employed at such salary. Transcripts from Foreign Universities: Prospective faculty submitting transcripts from foreign universities or schools must have the coursework evaluated for equivalency to United States-accredited coursework by a University-approved agency. The prospective faculty member is responsible for the cost of the evaluation. McNeese typically accepts evaluations by World Education Services ( www.wes.org ) or Educational Credential Evaluators, Inc. www.ece.org . McNeese State University offers a wide array of benefits to eligible employees to include: Comprehensive retirement programs through the State of Louisiana or Optional program, Supplemental retirement accounts (403B and 457) pre-tax and Roth versions, Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurance to include Vision, Life, Dental, Cancer, Intensive Care, Short Term Disability and more, Paid holidays, Tuition fee reduction program for eligible employees and dependents, Leave accrual and carryover, and many other on campus perks/discount programs. You may view the current year's Benefits Guide at: MYMCNEESE EMPLOYEE EXTRAS Employer McNeese State University Address McNeese State University Box 91615 Lake Charles, Louisiana, 70605 Phone (337) 475-5413 Website https://governmentjobs.com/careers/mcneese Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mcneese/jobs/5354874/clinical-director-clinical-assistant-professor-of-map": {
      "title": "Clinical Director/Clinical Assistant Professor of MAP",
      "description": "Clinical Director/Clinical Assistant Professor of MAP Salary $70,000.00 Annually Location 4205 Ryan St, Lake Charles, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number MSU052626U99809 Division Academic Affairs Opening Date 05/26/2026 Description Benefits Position/Application Information McNeese State University invites qualified applicants to apply for the position of Clinical Assistant Professor to serve as the Clinical Director of the McNeese Autism Program (MAP) and Assistant Professor of Psychology (Applied Behavior Analysis) in the Department of Psychology and Counseling/College of Nursing and Health Professions. This is a full-time, 12-month, unclassified, non-tenure track position beginning in August (Fall) 2026. In addition to clinical responsibilities, the candidate will hold the rank of Assistant Professor (non-tenure track) in the ABA master’s program, with a 2-2 teaching load. This position offers a unique opportunity to shape the next generation of scientist-practitioners in the field of ABA through student mentorship, supervision, high-quality instruction, and contributions to research and scholarship in the discipline. Position Number: U99809 Job Perks: Opportunities for salary supplement through paid summer teaching available upon request. Excellent fringe benefits including tuition reduction for employee, spouse, and dependent children; excellent healthcare benefits; and reimbursement for professional development needs such as CEUs towards mandatory BCBA/BCBA-D credential and conference travel. About the Program: The MAP clinic is an integral part of the on-campus Master of Science in Applied Behavior Analysis graduate program accredited by the Association for Behavior Analysis International Accreditation Board (ABAI), housed within the Department of Psychology and Counseling. The clinic provides high-quality ABA services to the community while serving as a premier training site for graduate and undergraduate students. Additional information about the Department of Psychology and Counseling can be viewed at www.mcneese.edu/nursing/psychology . Additional information about McNeese State University can be viewed at https://www.mcneese.edu/ . SALARY: $70,000 DEADLINE: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. APPLICATION PROCESS AND MATERIALS: For the application process, applicants MUST complete an electronic application and upload the required documents listed below: Letter of Application (Cover Letter) CV References (Name and contact information for at least three) Unofficial Transcripts (official transcripts will be required if hired) Finalists will be asked to submit a brief teaching sample Only completed application packets including all items listed above will be reviewed. ALL JOB OFFERS ARE CONTINGENT UPON THE SUCCESSFUL RESULT OF A CRIMINAL BACKGROUND CHECK AND RECEIPT OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT(S) IF APPLICABLE. TO APPLY FOR THIS VACANCY, click on the “APPLY” button at the top of advertisement to complete the electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future job opportunities. Applicants are responsible for checking the status of their application to determine where they are in the recruitment process. Further status message information is located under the Information section of the Current Job Opportunities page. CONTACT INFORMATION : QUESTIONS REGARDING THIS POSITION MAY BE DIRECTED TO THE CHAIR: Joanna B. Thompson, Ph.D., BCBA-D at jthompson2@mcneese.edu Kim Dronett, HR Analyst-Recruitment / Office of Human Resources / kdronett@mcneese.edu / (337) 475-5413 Position Duties/Responsibilities The successful candidate will serve as Clinical Director of our university-based Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA) clinic and must be a Board-Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) or BCBA-D. This role includes maintaining a 50% clinical practice commitment and collaborating with the Department of Psychology and Counseling’s on-campus, graduate program accredited by the Association for Behavior Analysis International Accreditation Board (ABAI) to support experiential learning. Key Responsibilities : Clinical Leadership (50%) – McNeese Autism Program (MAP) Clinical Director Service Delivery: Oversee all ABA services provided through the MAP on-campus clinic, ensuring adherence to evidence-based practices and ethical standards. Maintain a client caseload, conduct behavioral assessments, develop and monitor behavior intervention plans, and ensure documentation meets insurance and Medicaid requirements. The Clinical Director will oversee undergraduate and graduate students and collaborate with the Coordinator of Clinics to initiate purchase orders for supplies and equipment. Supervision & Management: Provide clinical supervision and mentorship to practicum and internship students in an ABAI accredited on-campus master’s program in ABA, as well as staff behavior analysts. Foster a collaborative and supportive team environment using behavioral skills training and ethical practice. Program Quality & Development: Set and monitor clinical performance goals, ensure high-quality service delivery, and maintain up-to-date knowledge of ABA best practices. Lead initiatives to expand services (e.g., social skills groups, telehealth) and training opportunities for students. Community Engagement: Organize and participate in community outreach and educational events to promote the MAP clinic and ABA services. Administrative Duties: Collaborate with the Coordinator of Clinics and other administrative staff to manage clinic operations, including scheduling, supply procurement, and compliance with HIPAA and other regulations. Serve as the ACE Provider for CEU events. Academic Faculty Responsibilities (50%) – Clinical Assistant Professor (NTT) Teaching: Teach on-campus graduate and undergraduate courses in ABA, with a standard 2-2 teaching load. Deliver high-quality, in-person instruction aligned with BACB and ABAI standards. Student Supervision: Supervise student research projects and provide practicum/internship supervision in accordance with BACB guidelines. Mentorship: Mentor students in the ABA program and support their professional development as behavior analysts consistent with a scientist-practitioner model. Scholarship & Service: Engage in scholarly activities, including opportunities for collaborative research within the MAP clinic. Participate in departmental, college, and university service, including committee work and accreditation efforts. Support ongoing lines of research and/or develop new lines of scholarly research for presentation. Collaborate with the Director of the Applied Behavior Analysis Master’s Program. Required/Preferred Qualifications Minimum Qualifications : Doctoral degree in Psychology, Applied Behavior Analysis, or a closely related field (ABD considered). Current certification as a Board-Certified Behavior Analyst (BCBA) or BCBA-D. Must be eligible to supervise. Eligible for licensure in the State of Louisiana. Demonstrated experience in clinical service delivery, supervision, and teaching in ABA. Commitment to ethical practice, diversity, and student-centered education. Eligibility to serve as an ACE Provider for CEU events is preferred. General University information McNeese State University, located in Lake Charles, Louisiana, is a public university and a member of the University of Louisiana System. Under Louisiana law, applications and all supporting materials will become public record. All applicants are expected to submit complete and accurate materials as specified in the position announcement. A background check and an English Proficiency assessment (Faculty Only) will be conducted on selected finalists. We comply with Louisiana Revised Statute 49:1001, et seq, and State of Louisiana Executive Order 98-38, which provides for drug testing of employees, appointees, prospective employees, and prospective appointees. Prospective employees and employees are informed if a drug test is required. McNeese State University is an AA/EEO/ADA employer committed to excellence through diversity and a SAME agency (State as a Model Employer for People with Disabilities) for the State of Louisiana. Persons needing reasonable accommodations as provided by the Americans with Disabilities Act should contact the ADA Coordinator, Krisshunn Youngblood, Office of Campus Compliance and Civility at (337) 475-5428 or kyoungblood@mcneese.edu . The Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 requires McNeese State University to inform applicants that the University can employ only U.S. citizens and aliens lawfully authorized to work in the U.S. Each new employee is required to present documentation verifying his/her identity and right to accept employment. McNeese participates in E-Verify. Louisiana Revised Statute 42:31-“Eligibility requirements for certain unclassified employees”-requires any person hired or employed in an unclassified position, whose annual salary or rate of compensation is equal to or exceeds one hundred thousand dollars, provide proof to his public employer that he has been issued a Louisiana driver’s license and that all vehicles registered in his name are registered in Louisiana within thirty days of being hired or employed at such salary. Transcripts from Foreign Universities: Prospective faculty submitting transcripts from foreign universities or schools must have the coursework evaluated for equivalency to United States-accredited coursework by a University-approved agency. The prospective faculty member is responsible for the cost of the evaluation. McNeese typically accepts evaluations by World Education Services ( www.wes.org ) or Educational Credential Evaluators, Inc. www.ece.org . McNeese State University offers a wide array of benefits to eligible employees to include: Comprehensive retirement programs through the State of Louisiana or Optional program, Supplemental retirement accounts (403B and 457) pre-tax and Roth versions, Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurance to include Vision, Life, Dental, Cancer, Intensive Care, Short Term Disability and more, Paid holidays, Tuition fee reduction program for eligible employees and dependents, Leave accrual and carryover, and many other on campus perks/discount programs. You may view the current year's Benefits Guide at: MYMCNEESE EMPLOYEE EXTRAS Employer McNeese State University Address McNeese State University Box 91615 Lake Charles, Louisiana, 70605 Phone (337) 475-5413 Website https://governmentjobs.com/careers/mcneese Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mcneese/jobs/5488225/constituent-relationship-management-crm-administrator": {
      "title": "Constituent Relationship Management (CRM) Administrator",
      "description": "Constituent Relationship Management (CRM) Administrator Salary $45,000.00 Annually Location 4205 Ryan St, Lake Charles, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number MSU091826U99140 Division Enrollment Management Opening Date 09/18/2026 Description Benefits Position/Application Information McNeese State University invites applicants for the position of Constituent Relationship Management (CRM) Administrator in the Office of Recruiting. This is a full-time, 12–month, unclassified staff position. The appointment is available immediately. Position Number: U99140 SALARY: $45,000 REPORTING AUTHORITY: Director of Recruiting DEADLINE: Position will remain open until filled. APPLICATION PROCESS AND MATERIALS: For the application process, applicants MUST complete an electronic application and upload required documents listed below: Letter of Application (Cover Letter) Resume Three (3) Professional References (include: name, phone number, and e-mail address) Unofficial Transcripts O nly completed application packets including all items listed above will be reviewed. ALL JOB OFFERS ARE CONTINGENT UPON THE SUCCESSFUL RESULT OF A CRIMINAL BACKGROUND CHECK AND RECEIPT OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT(S) IF APPLICABLE. TO APPLY FOR THIS VACANCY, click on the “APPLY” button at the top of advertisement to complete the electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future job opportunities. Applicants are responsible for checking the status of their application to determine where they are in the recruitment process. Further status message information is located under the Information section of the Current Job Opportunities page. * Required application materials WILL NOT be accepted after the deadline, if applicable. Applications may be rejected if incomplete. CONTACT INFORMATION: QUESTIONS REGARDING THIS POSITION MAY BE DIRECTED TO THE CHAIR: Madeline Nash at mstark3@mcneese.edu Office of Human Resources Contact : Kim Dronett, HR Analyst/Employment Liaison: kdronett@mcneese.edu or (337) 475-5413 Position Duties/Responsibilities Manage data migrations, imports, integrity and manipulation tasks. This includes building and maintaining crosswalks/data translation, identifying, researching and troubleshooting feed errors, and inspecting and correcting data files Perform database management including hygiene, segmentation, targeting and troubleshooting within Recruit (CRM) and other related technology solutions Develop and maintain custom reports, dashboards, maintain validation rules and custom processes/flows. Create and manage custom objects, fields, and formulas. Create and manage field dependencies, conditional logic and assignment rules on all user-facing forms Analyze CRM processes and procedures and prepare recommendations for improvements and develop customized solutions within the Recruit platform to ensure that critical business functions are supported, project objectives and college goals are met, and business needs are addressed with efficient, effective solutions. This includes determining and documenting business user requirements and performing hands-on solution design, prototyping, and proof-of-concepts, as required in support of current and new CRM projects Work with internal and external staff to use the CRM in an efficient, effective manner. Identify best practices in the use of Recruit CRM and disseminate them to end users. Manage access rights for staff and consultants for the CRM system. Provide high-quality end user support to users of Recruit CRM Participate with the Integration Developers on integrations to/from Recruit and other CRM systems with other enterprise systems Help establish long-term strategic goals for high-quality data and effective data usage Collaborate and work in conjunction with the offices of Enrollment Management and the Office of Marketing and Public Relations to ensure automated communications have a consistent voice, cohesive messaging, branding and design, and current, live links to support and engagement resources for constituents. Collaborate and work in conjunction with Enrollment Management to develop, implement and refine a comprehensive communications plan for prospective students, parents, counselors and other targeted audiences from the initial contact phase to the student orientation phase Required/Preferred Qualifications Required : Bachelor’s degree - required (from a regionally accredited institution) Excellent written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative team Demonstrated flexibility to adapt to rapidly changing demands and priorities Demonstrated organizational skills and attention to deadlines in a fast-paced work setting General University information McNeese State University, located in Lake Charles, Louisiana, is a public university and a member of the University of Louisiana System. Under Louisiana law, applications and all supporting materials will become public record. All applicants are expected to submit complete and accurate materials as specified in the position announcement. A background check and an English Proficiency assessment (Faculty Only) will be conducted on selected finalists. We comply with Louisiana Revised Statute 49:1001, et seq, and State of Louisiana Executive Order 98-38, which provides for drug testing of employees, appointees, prospective employees, and prospective appointees. Prospective employees and employees are informed if a drug test is required. McNeese State University is an AA/EEO/ADA employer committed to excellence through diversity and a SAME agency (State as a Model Employer for People with Disabilities) for the State of Louisiana. Persons needing reasonable accommodations as provided by the Americans with Disabilities Act should contact the ADA Coordinator, Dr. Desmond Wallace, Office of Inclusive Excellence: Voice: (337) 475-5428; TDD/TTY, Hearing Impaired: (337) 562-4227; or dwallace@mcneese.edu . The Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 requires McNeese State University to inform applicants that the University can employ only U.S. citizens and aliens lawfully authorized to work in the U.S. Each new employee is required to present documentation verifying his/her identity and right to accept employment. McNeese participates in E-Verify. Louisiana Revised Statute 42:31-“Eligibility requirements for certain unclassified employees”-requires any person hired or employed in an unclassified position, whose annual salary or rate of compensation is equal to or exceeds one hundred thousand dollars, provide proof to his public employer that he has been issued a Louisiana driver’s license and that all vehicles registered in his name are registered in Louisiana within thirty days of being hired or employed at such salary. Transcripts from Foreign Universities: Prospective faculty submitting transcripts from foreign universities or schools must have the coursework evaluated for equivalency to United States-accredited coursework by a university-approved agency. The prospective faculty member is responsible for the cost of the evaluation. McNeese typically accepts evaluations by World Education Services ( www.wes.org ) or Educational Credential Evaluators, Inc. www.ece.org . McNeese State University offers a wide array of benefits to eligible employees to include: Comprehensive retirement programs through the State of Louisiana or Optional program, Supplemental retirement accounts (403B and 457) pre-tax and Roth versions, Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurance to include Vision, Life, Dental, Cancer, Intensive Care, Short Term Disability and more, Paid holidays, Tuition fee reduction program for eligible employees and dependents, Leave accrual and carryover, and many other on campus perks/discount programs. You may view the current year's Benefits Guide at: MYMCNEESE EMPLOYEE EXTRAS Employer McNeese State University Address McNeese State University Box 91615 Lake Charles, Louisiana, 70605 Phone (337) 475-5413 Website https://governmentjobs.com/careers/mcneese Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mcneese/jobs/5430394/director-of-human-resources-and-student-employment": {
      "title": "Director of Human Resources and Student Employment",
      "description": "Director of Human Resources and Student Employment Location 4205 Ryan St, Lake Charles, LA Job Type Full-Time Job Number MSU073026U99945 Division Business Affairs Opening Date 07/30/2026 Description Benefits Position/Application Information McNeese State University invites applicants for the position of Director of Human Resources and Student Employment in the Office of Human Resources and Student Employment. This is a full-time, 12-month, unclassified, staff position. The appointment is available to begin immediately. Position Number: U99945 SALARY: Commensurate with education and experience. POSITION SUMMARY: The Director of Human Resources and Student Employment provides strategic and operational leadership for all human resources and student employment functions at the university. This position ensures institutional compliance with applicable federal and state employment laws, University of Louisiana System policies, and university procedures, while actively supporting the university’s mission and core values. The Director reports to the Vice President for Business Affairs and serves as the principal advisor to executive leadership on all HR-related matters, oversees a team of HR professionals, and champions a workplace culture defined by equity, professionalism, accountability, and service excellence. This role requires a high degree of discretion, sound judgment, and the ability to navigate complex personnel, legal, and organizational challenges with integrity and care. DEADLINE: Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain open until position is filled. APPLICATION PROCESS AND MATERIALS: For the application process, applicants MUST complete an electronic application and upload required documents listed below: Cover Letter Resume Three Professional References (Include: name, phone number, and email address) Unofficial Transcripts for all degrees earned O nly completed application packets including all items listed above will be reviewed. ALL JOB OFFERS ARE CONTINGENT UPON THE SUCCESSFUL RESULT OF A CRIMINAL BACKGROUND CHECK AND RECEIPT OF OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT(S) IF APPLICABLE. TO APPLY FOR THIS VACANCY, click on the “APPLY” button at the top of advertisement to complete the electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future job opportunities. Applicants are responsible for checking the status of their application to determine where they are in the recruitment process. Further status message information is located under the Information section of the Current Job Opportunities page. * Required application materials WILL NOT be accepted after the deadline, if applicable. Applications may be rejected if incomplete. CONTACT INFORMATION : QUESTIONS REGARDING THIS POSITION MAY BE DIRECTED TO THE CHAIR: April Broussard, Vice President for Business Affairs at abroussard1@mcneese.edu Office of Human Resources Contact: Kim Dronett, HR Analyst/Recruitment kdronett@mcneese.edu or (337) 475-5413 Position Duties/Responsibilities Leadership and Departmental Administration Direct, manage, and evaluate all operations of the Office of Human Resources and Student Employment, including supervision, mentoring, and performance evaluation of departmental staff. Provide strategic guidance and counsel to the Vice President for Business Affairs, executive leadership, supervisors, and employees on a full range of human resources matters. Establish and maintain departmental policies, procedures, internal controls, and budget management in accordance with university fiscal and operational standards. Serve on institutional committees as required and assist the Vice President for Business Affairs with special projects and initiatives as needed. Recruitment, Hiring, and Workforce Management Oversee all recruitment, hiring, onboarding, and offboarding processes for classified, unclassified, faculty, adjunct, and student employment categories in compliance with applicable laws, policies, and requirements. Develop and maintain onboarding and separation procedures to ensure timely processing of personnel actions and proper documentation of employment records. Compensation, Benefits, and Retirement Administer employee benefits, retirement programs (including TRSL, LASERS, and ORP), and ancillary benefits; serve as primary liaison with applicable state agencies and benefit providers. Ensure accurate and timely processing of payroll and personnel actions in Banner and applicable state systems; review and approve PAFs, reclassifications, salary adjustments, and position control changes. Employee Relations and Compliance Serve as Delegated Appointing Authority for classified employees, overseeing disciplinary processes, grievances, and adverse actions in compliance with Louisiana Civil Service rules. Represent the university in administrative hearings, unemployment proceedings, and legal matters involving human resources as required. Investigate employee complaints and potential policy violations; recommend and implement appropriate corrective actions. Ensure compliance with all applicable federal and state employment laws, including Title VII, ADA, ADEA, FMLA, FLSA, Title IX, and Louisiana Civil Service statutes; develop and maintain HR policies and procedures accordingly. Leave, Workers’ Compensation, and Safety Administer the FMLA program and oversee the university’s workers’ compensation program, including claims management, return-to-work coordination, and required reporting. Coordinate workplace safety programs and injury prevention initiatives in compliance with applicable OSHA and state safety regulations. Training, Immigration, Systems, and Reporting Manage new employee orientation and coordinate training programs for supervisors and staff on performance management, compliance, workplace conduct, and HR systems. Oversee immigration processes for international employees and faculty, including visa sponsorships and work authorization compliance. Maintain HR information systems and personnel records in compliance with applicable records retention schedules, privacy regulations, and institutional policy. Oversee internal and external HR audits and prepare required regulatory reports, including EEO-1, IPEDS human resources components, and other applicable state and federal submissions. Student Employment Oversee the university’s student employment program, ensuring compliance with federal work-study requirements, institutional policies, and applicable wage and hour laws. Coordinate with Financial Aid and department supervisors to facilitate student placements, process personnel actions, and resolve employment-related concerns. Required/Preferred Qualifications Education Bachelor’s degree required in Human Resources Management, Business Administration, Public Administration, or a closely related field Master’s degree preferred (MBA, MPA, Master’s in Human Resources, or Master’s in Organizational Leadership) Professional HR certification preferred: PHR, SPHR, SHRM-CP, or SHRM-SCP Experience Minimum 5 years of progressively responsible human resources experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience Proven leadership and team management skills, with direct supervisory responsibility over professional HR staff Demonstrated experience overseeing a broad range of HR functions including recruitment, employee relations, benefits, payroll coordination, and compliance Prior experience in higher education or public sector HR strongly preferred Experience with Louisiana Civil Service rules and regulations preferred General University information McNeese State University, located in Lake Charles, Louisiana, is a public university and a member of the University of Louisiana System. Under Louisiana law, applications and all supporting materials will become public record. All applicants are expected to submit complete and accurate materials as specified in the position announcement. A background check and an English Proficiency assessment (Faculty Only) will be conducted on selected finalists. We comply with Louisiana Revised Statute 49:1001, et seq, and State of Louisiana Executive Order 98-38, which provides for drug testing of employees, appointees, prospective employees, and prospective appointees. Prospective employees and employees are informed if a drug test is required. McNeese State University is an AA/EEO/ADA employer committed to excellence through diversity and a SAME agency (State as a Model Employer for People with Disabilities) for the State of Louisiana. Persons requesting accommodations in accordance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) should contact the Office of Campus Compliance and Civility at least 72 hours before the event. Additional information is available from the Office of Campus Compliance and Civility, located in the Burton Business Center, Suite 407, by phone at 337-475-5428, by fax at 337-475-5603, or by email at compliance@mcneese.edu . The Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986 requires McNeese State University to inform applicants that the University can employ only U.S. citizens and aliens lawfully authorized to work in the U.S. Each new employee is required to present documentation verifying his/her identity and right to accept employment. McNeese participates in E-Verify. Louisiana Revised Statute 42:31-“Eligibility requirements for certain unclassified employees”-requires any person hired or employed in an unclassified position, whose annual salary or rate of compensation is equal to or exceeds one hundred thousand dollars, provide proof to his public employer that he has been issued a Louisiana driver’s license and that all vehicles registered in his name are registered in Louisiana within thirty days of being hired or employed at such salary. Transcripts from Foreign Universities: Prospective faculty submitting transcripts from foreign universities or schools must have the coursework evaluated for equivalency to United States-accredited coursework by a University-approved agency. The prospective faculty member is responsible for the cost of the evaluation. McNeese typically accepts evaluations by World Education Services ( www.wes.org ) or Educational Credential Evaluators, Inc. www.ece.org . McNeese State University offers a wide array of benefits to eligible employees to include: Comprehensive retirement programs through the State of Louisiana or Optional program, Supplemental retirement accounts (403B and 457) pre-tax and Roth versions, Health Insurance, Life Insurance, Supplemental Insurance to include Vision, Life, Dental, Cancer, Intensive Care, Short Term Disability and more, Paid holidays, Tuition fee reduction program for eligible employees and dependents, Leave accrual and carryover, and many other on campus perks/discount programs. You may view the current year's Benefits Guide at: MYMCNEESE EMPLOYEE EXTRAS Employer McNeese State University Address McNeese State University Box 91615 Lake Charles, Louisiana, 70605 Phone (337) 475-5413 Website https://governmentjobs.com/careers/mcneese Apply"
